#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# hyperfactorial

#% text
# `hyperfactorial(n)` gives the product 1^1 2^2 ... n^n.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Exact for non-negative integers up to 2000.
#% item
# Other numbers continue it as the K-function `exp(zeta'(-1, z + 1) - zeta'(-1))` (DLMF 5.17), with principal logarithms in the defining sum of the Hurwitz zeta function: real for `z >= -1` and at the integers, complex for non-integer `z < -1`; `hyperfactorial(-n)` is `(-1)^(n (n - 1)/2) hyperfactorial(n - 1)`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
hyperfactorial(3)
#% output
#= 108

#% cell
map(hyperfactorial, range(0, 5))
#% output
#= [1, 1, 4, 108, 27648, 86400000]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `factorial`
